0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Z80
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Three switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    EDITOR   1 = with the line editor built in (see the end of this file):
0000                             ;                 the spec's suggested standard. It goes with either setting
0000                             ;                 of the other two.
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), Z80 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   1   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                EDITOR:   EQU   0   ; 1 = with the line editor
0000                EDGEN:    EQU   EDITOR*(1-CPM)   ; (the generic build with the editor)
0000                             ; (IF takes any value but 0 as true, so
0000                             ;  IF CHECKED+EDITOR means "either")
0000                TABP0:    EQU   EDGEN*(1-CHECKED)   ; (the build with its table in page zero)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the Z80"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    HL'  return-stack pointer (the alternate HL). Entries are 2 bytes; the
0000                             ;         stack grows down. Only rpop and rpushn (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 08h  rpop    pop the return stack into DE
0000                             ;    RST 18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 18h and RST 30h never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing
0000                             ;  each of them does is POP DE to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block is written to work at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
0000                BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
0000                BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
                    KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
                                 ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
                                 ;   (end the routine with OR A / RET).
                    CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
                                 ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE, HL and HL'.
                    RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
                    DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
                    LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
                    PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
                    HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
                    BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0FF09h   ; where the editor's ^X goes
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0000h   ; the editor's ^X: warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR   
                    EXIT:     EQU   edend   ; a program that ends goes back to the editor,
                    SKEND:    EQU   skend   ;   also when it ends inside skip
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0000                SKEND:    EQU   EXIT   
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. (The wait
0000                             ; for a second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms.)
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSAVE:    EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: return stack pointer, saved
0000                             ;   around machine code;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                EDLN:     EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the editor: the number of the line that ^E
0000                             ;   put in the input line (0: none)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; gap after z: a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0100                          .ORG   BASE   
0100                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset. (This byte, AFh, is also what an
0100                          ENDIF      ;     undefined word runs into: see e_hi.)
0100                          IF   1-EDGEN   
0100   31 FC 07               LD   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; 03  the IP
                              JR   st0   ; 06  (the rest of the startup is close by)
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              JR   init   ; 04  (the rest of the startup is close by)
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   EDGEN   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset: no program yet. (This byte, AFh,
                              LD   (PROG),A   ;     is also what an undefined word runs
                              JP   init   ; 04  into in the checked build: see e_hi.)
                              NOP      ; 07  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   CPM   
0103   C3 A8 05               JP   start   ; 03
0106   00 00                  DW   0   ; 06  spare
0108                          ENDIF      
0108                VECS:        
0108                             ; ---- RST 08h: rpop: pop the return stack into DE ---------------------------
0108   D9           RPOP:     EXX      ; 08
0109   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
010A   23                     INC   HL   
010B   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
010C   23                     INC   HL   
010D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; across to the main registers
010E   D9                     EXX      
010F   D1                     POP   DE   
0110   C9                     RET      ; 10  (so RST 10h is not used)
0111                             ; ctl: the inner loop comes here for characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0111   C6 21        CTL:      ADD   A,21h   ; 11  back to c; zero only for NUL
0113   20 1F                  JR   NZ,next0   ;     the rest are ignored
0115   C3 00 00     ENDPROG:   JP   EXIT   ;     the program has ended
0118                             ; ---- RST 18h: drop TOS, then next ------------------------------------------
0118   D1           RST18:    POP   DE   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0119   E1                     POP   HL   ;     new TOS = NOS
011A   18 15                  JR   nx   
011C   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   HL   ; 1C  "}" return stack to TOS
011D   CF                     RST   08h   
011E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
011F   F7                     RST   30h   
0120                             ; ---- RST 20h: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) -------------------------------
0120   AF           NEG16:    XOR   A   ; 20
0121   95                     SUB   L   
0122   6F                     LD   L,A   
0123   9F                     SBC   A,A   
0124   94                     SUB   H   
0125   67                     LD   H,A   
0126   C9                     RET      
0127   00                     NOP      ; 27  spare
0128                             ; ---- RST 28h: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL, HL') ------------------------
0128                RST28:       
0128                          IFN   CPM   
                    PUTC:     JP   CONOUT   ; 28
0128                          ENDIF      
0128                          IF   CPM   
0128   C3 29 04               JP   putc   ; 28
012B                          ENDIF      
012B   E9           JPHL:     JP   (HL)   ; 2B  (for the machine-code call)
012C   E3           H_TOR:    EX   (SP),HL   ; 2C  "{" TOS to the return stack: the new TOS
012D   C3 C9 01               JP   rpushn   ;     comes up, the old one goes across
0130                             ; ---- RST 30h: next character -----------------------------------------------
0130   D1           RST30:    POP   DE   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0131                NX:          
0131                          IF   CPM   
0131   C3 34 01               JP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0134                          ENDIF      
0134                VECEND:      
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0134                             ; 
0134                             ;    00h          end of program
0134                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0134                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0134                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0134                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0134                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                NEXT0:       
0134                          IF   CHECKED   
0134   CD 6F 04               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0137                          ENDIF      
0137   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0138   03                     INC   BC   
0139   D6 21                  SUB   21h   ; A = c - 21h
013B   38 D4                  JR   C,ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
013D   FE 0F                  CP   0Fh   
013F   38 25                  JR   C,punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
0141   D6 0F                  SUB   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0143   FE 0A                  CP   0Ah   
0145   38 6C                  JR   C,digit   ; 30h-39h
0147   FE 11                  CP   11h   
0149   38 19                  JR   C,p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
014B   D6 11                  SUB   11h   ; A = c - 41h
014D   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   
014F   38 6E                  JR   C,upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
0151   FE 20                  CP   20h   
0153   38 0D                  JR   C,p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0155   FE 3A                  CP   3Ah   
0157   38 60                  JR   C,lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0159   FE 3E                  CP   3Eh   
015B                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JR   NC,next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
015B                          ENDIF      
015B                          IF   CHECKED   
015B   28 D7                  JR   Z,next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
015D   D2 9C 04               JP   NC,e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
0160                          ENDIF      
0160   D6 1A                  SUB   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
0162   D6 09        P5B:      SUB   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
0164   C6 05        P3A:      ADD   A,5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
0166                .macro PTABLE,
0166                             ; 
0166                 DB      h_store & 0FFh  ; !
0166                 DB      h_str & 0FFh    ; "
0166                 DB      h_num & 0FFh    ; #
0166                 DB      h_print & 0FFh  ; $
0166                 DB      h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0166                 DB      h_and & 0FFh    ; &
0166                 DB      h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0166                 DB      h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0166                 DB      h_close & 0FFh  ; )
0166                 DB      h_mul & 0FFh    ; *
0166                 DB      h_add & 0FFh    ; +
0166                 DB      h_cfetch & 0FFh ; ,
0166                 DB      h_sub & 0FFh    ; -
0166                 DB      h_cstore & 0FFh ; .
0166                 DB      h_div & 0FFh    ; /
0166                 DB      h_dup & 0FFh    ; :
0166                 DB      h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0166                 DB      h_lt & 0FFh     ; <
0166                 DB      h_eq & 0FFh     ; =
0166                 DB      h_gt & 0FFh     ; >
0166                 DB      h_key & 0FFh    ; ?
0166                 DB      h_fetch & 0FFh  ; @
0166                 DB      h_def & 0FFh    ; [
0166                 DB      h_break & 0FFh  ; \
0166                 DB      h_ret & 0FFh    ; ]
0166                 DB      h_xor & 0FFh    ; ^
0166                 DB      h_alloc & 0FFh  ; _
0166                 DB      h_grave & 0FFh  ; `
0166                 DB      h_tor & 0FFh    ; {
0166                 DB      h_or & 0FFh     ; |
0166                 DB      h_fromr & 0FFh  ; }
0166                 DB      h_not & 0FFh    ; ~
0166                .endm
0166                 
0166                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
0166                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
0166   C6 B3        PUNCT:    ADD   A,PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0168   5F                     LD   E,A   
0169   16 03                  LD   D,PTAB / 256   ; (0 if the table is in page zero)
016B   FE C9                  CP   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
016D   1A                     LD   A,(DE)   
016E   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
016F                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-TABP0)   
                              LD   D,0   
016F                          ENDIF      
016F                          IFN   CPM   
                              RL   D   ; its page: 0 + carry
016F                          ENDIF      
016F                          IF   CPM   
016F   16 01                  LD   D,1   
0171   30 01                  JR   NC,pu1   
0173   14                     INC   D   ; its page: 1 + carry
0174                PU1:         
0174                          ENDIF      
0174   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
0175   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
0176                             ; The rest of the startup: here so that the generic reset code can reach it
0176                             ; with JR. st0: find the program's NUL; the heap starts after it.
0176                             ; (The editor build has its own copy of this, next to the editor.)
0176                             ; A checked build first clears the lower half of the letter page (A = 0):
0176                             ; every variable starts at 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an
0176                             ; undefined word is caught at (see e_hi), and no key is held back.
0176                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                    INIT:     LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
0176                          ENDIF      
0176                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    ST0:      LD   H,B   
                              LD   L,C   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
0176                          ENDIF      
0176                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0176   22 7C 08     ST2:      LD   (HEAP),HL   
0179                          ENDIF      
0179                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
0179   E7                     RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
017A   22 38 08               LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
017D                          ENDIF      
017D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                              LD   HL,0   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ;   (the checked build has cleared these)
017D                          ENDIF      
017D                          IF   1-EDITOR   
017D   D9                     EXX      
017E   21 E0 06               LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
0181   D9                     EXX      
0182   F7                     RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
0183                          ENDIF      
0183                             ; In the unchecked generic editor build the table is here, in the first
0183                             ; page, which saves loading D twice. (The other builds have no room for it
0183                             ; here: theirs is further down.)
0183                          IF   TABP0   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
0183                          ENDIF      
0183                             ; =============================================================================
0183                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0183                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.) The machine-code call, exec,
0183                             ;  is here too: it belongs to "`" and makes the page come out right.
0183                             ; =============================================================================
0183   D1           H_XOR:    POP   DE   
0184   7C                     LD   A,H   
0185   AA                     XOR   D   
0186   67                     LD   H,A   
0187   7D                     LD   A,L   
0188   AB                     XOR   E   
0189   6F                     LD   L,A   
018A   F7                     RST   30h   
018B   D1           H_OR:     POP   DE   
018C   7C                     LD   A,H   
018D   B2                     OR   D   
018E   67                     LD   H,A   
018F   7D                     LD   A,L   
0190   B3                     OR   E   
0191   6F                     LD   L,A   
0192   F7                     RST   30h   
0193   E7           H_NOT:    RST   20h   ; ~x = -x - 1
0194   2B                     DEC   HL   
0195   F7                     RST   30h   
0196                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0196                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0196   ED 5B 7C 08  H_ALLOC:   LD   DE,(HEAP)   
019A                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
019A   7C                     LD   A,H   ; the count's sign, for chkhp
019B                          ENDIF      
019B   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the new top
019C                          IF   CHECKED   
019C   CD 53 04               CALL   chkhp   
019F                          ENDIF      
019F   22 7C 08               LD   (HEAP),HL   
01A2   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
01A3   F7                     RST   30h   
01A4   D9           EXEC:     EXX      
01A5   22 34 08               LD   (RSAVE),HL   ; machine code may change the alternates
01A8   D9                     EXX      
01A9   CD 2B 01               CALL   jphl   
01AC   D9                     EXX      
01AD   2A 34 08               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
01B0   D9                     EXX      
01B1   E1                     POP   HL   
01B2   F7                     RST   30h   
01B3                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
01B3                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
01B3                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
01B3   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
01B4   0B                     DEC   BC   
01B5   CD 35 03               CALL   rdnum   
01B8   F7                     RST   30h   
01B9                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
01B9   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
01BA   87                     ADD   A,A   
01BB   6F                     LD   L,A   
01BC   26 08                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
01BE   F7                     RST   30h   
01BF                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
01BF                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
01BF   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
01C0   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
01C1   87                     ADD   A,A   
01C2   6F                     LD   L,A   
01C3   26 08                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
01C5   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
01C6   2C                     INC   L   
01C7   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
01C8   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
01C9                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
01C9                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
01C9                             ; 
01C9                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
01C9                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
01C9                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
01C9                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop two bytes and 13 T-states.
01C9   D9           RPUSHN:   EXX      
01CA   D1                     POP   DE   
01CB   2B                     DEC   HL   
01CC   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01CD   2B                     DEC   HL   
01CE   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01CF   10 05                  DJNZ   rp1   
01D1   D9                     EXX      
01D2   CD E5 03               CALL   pollk   
01D5   F7                     RST   30h   
01D6   D9           RP1:      EXX      
01D7   F7                     RST   30h   
01D8                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
01D8                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
01D8                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
01D8                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
01D8                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
01D8                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
01D8                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
01D8   CD D3 03     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
01DB   30 C7                  JR   NC,exec   
01DD   77           HX1:      LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
01DE   CD D3 03               CALL   hexc   
01E1   30 08                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
01E3   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
01E5   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
01E6   CD D3 03               CALL   hexc   
01E9   38 F2                  JR   C,hx1   
01EB   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
01ED   F7                     RST   30h   
01EE                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01EE                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01EE                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01EE                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01EE                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01EE                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
01EE   CF           H_RET:    RST   08h   
01EF   42                     LD   B,D   
01F0   4B                     LD   C,E   
01F1   F7           BRK1:     RST   30h   
01F2                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
01F2                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
01F2   7C           H_BREAK:   LD   A,H   
01F3   B5                     OR   L   
01F4   E1                     POP   HL   
01F5   28 FA                  JR   Z,brk1   
01F7   CD 5C 03               CALL   skip   
01FA   B7                     OR   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
01FB   20 F1                  JR   NZ,h_ret   
01FD   CF           RDROP:    RST   08h   
01FE   F7                     RST   30h   
01FF                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
01FF                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
01FF                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
01FF                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
01FF                             ; checked build stops on it.)
01FF   0A           H_DEF:    LD   A,(BC)   
0200   03                     INC   BC   
0201   D6 41                  SUB   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
0203   5F                     LD   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
0204   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   ; fold case
0206   FE 1A                  CP   26   
0208   30 0B                  JR   NC,def2   ; not a letter
020A   CB 23                  SLA   E   
020C   16 08                  LD   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
020E   79                     LD   A,C   
020F   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0210   1C                     INC   E   
0211   78                     LD   A,B   
0212   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0213   18 09                  JR   skipnx   
0215                DEF2:        
0215                          IF   CHECKED   
0215   7B                     LD   A,E   
0216   FE DF                  CP   " "-"A"+256   
0218   C2 BC 04               JP   NZ,e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
021B                          ENDIF      
021B   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; an anonymous block: push its address
021C   60                     LD   H,B   
021D   69                     LD   L,C   
021E                SKIPNX:      
021E                          IF   CHECKED   
021E   0B                     DEC   BC   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
021F                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
021F   CD 5C 03     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
0222   F7                     RST   30h   
0223   5E           H_FETCH:   LD   E,(HL)   ; "@"
0224   23                     INC   HL   
0225   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0226   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0227   F7                     RST   30h   
0228                             ; =============================================================================
0228                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0228                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it), so its long tail may run past that
0228                             ;  page.
0228                             ; =============================================================================
0228                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0228                             ; the matching ")".
0228   7C           H_OPEN:   LD   A,H   
0229   B5                     OR   L   
022A   E1                     POP   HL   
022B   28 F2                  JR   Z,skipo   
022D   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the block starts at the IP
022E   18 99                  JR   rpushn   
0230                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
0230                             ; drops it and carries on.
0230   7C           H_CLOSE:   LD   A,H   
0231   B5                     OR   L   
0232   E1                     POP   HL   
0233   28 C8                  JR   Z,rdrop   
0235   CF                     RST   08h   ; pop the block start ...
0236   42                     LD   B,D   
0237   4B                     LD   C,E   
0238   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0239   18 8E                  JR   rpushn   ; ... and push it back
023B                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
023B                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
023B   0A           H_SUB:    LD   A,(BC)   
023C   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
023E   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0240   38 04                  JR   C,negnum   
0242   E7                     RST   20h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
0243   D1           H_ADD:    POP   DE   
0244   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0245   F7                     RST   30h   
0246   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   HL   ; a negative number: read it, negate it
0247   CD 35 03               CALL   rdnum   
024A   E7                     RST   20h   
024B   F7                     RST   30h   
024C   D1           H_AND:    POP   DE   
024D   7C                     LD   A,H   
024E   A2                     AND   D   
024F   67                     LD   H,A   
0250   7D                     LD   A,L   
0251   A3                     AND   E   
0252   6F                     LD   L,A   
0253   F7                     RST   30h   
0254                             ; Signed compares. Both are "HL < DE" for the right pair: "<" swaps the two
0254                             ; cells first. Flipping both sign bits turns a signed compare into an
0254                             ; unsigned one (and XOR clears the carry for SBC); SBC HL,HL then turns the
0254                             ; carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
0254   E3           H_LT:     EX   (SP),HL   ; a < b: HL = a, and b is popped next
0255   D1           H_GT:     POP   DE   ; a > b  is  b < a: HL = b, DE = a
0256   7C                     LD   A,H   
0257   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0259   67                     LD   H,A   
025A   7A                     LD   A,D   
025B   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
025D   57                     LD   D,A   
025E   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry if HL < DE
0260   ED 62        TF:       SBC   HL,HL   ; carry -> -1 or 0
0262   F7                     RST   30h   
0263   D1           H_EQ:     POP   DE   
0264   B7                     OR   A   
0265   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0267   7C                     LD   A,H   
0268   B5                     OR   L   
0269   FE 01                  CP   1   ; carry only if a - b = 0
026B   18 F3                  JR   tf   
026D                             ; "*": shift-and-add, 16 rounds; only the low 16 bits are kept. The
026D                             ; multiplier shifts up through A:C.
026D   D1           H_MUL:    POP   DE   ; DE = multiplicand
026E   C5                     PUSH   BC   
026F   7C                     LD   A,H   
0270   4D                     LD   C,L   ; A:C = multiplier
0271   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
0274   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0276   29           MUL1:     ADD   HL,HL   
0277   CB 21                  SLA   C   
0279   17                     RLA      
027A   30 01                  JR   NC,mul2   
027C   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
027D   10 F7        MUL2:     DJNZ   mul1   
027F   C1                     POP   BC   
0280   F7                     RST   30h   
0281                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
0281                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
0281                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
0281                             ; stops on it.
0281                H_DIV:       
0281                          IF   CHECKED   
0281   7C                     LD   A,H   
0282   B5                     OR   L   
0283   CA B9 04               JP   Z,e_zero   
0286                          ENDIF      
0286   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
0287   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; free BC for udiv
0288   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; a, for r's sign
0289   7A                     LD   A,D   
028A   AC                     XOR   H   
028B   F5                     PUSH   AF   ; S flag = sign of q
028C   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
028E   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |b|
0291   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0292   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0294   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
0297   CD 0F 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, DE = r
029A   F1                     POP   AF   
029B   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; q's sign
029E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; HL = r, DE = q
029F   F1                     POP   AF   ; A = a's high byte
02A0   B7                     OR   A   
02A1   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; r's sign
02A4   C1                     POP   BC   
02A5   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; q under r
02A6   F7                     RST   30h   
02A7                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
02A7   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   HL   ; ":"
02A8   F7                     RST   30h   
02A9   E3           H_SWAP:   EX   (SP),HL   ; "%"
02AA   F7                     RST   30h   
02AB                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
02AB                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
02AB                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
02AB                          IF   CHECKED   
02AB   CD 42 04               CALL   chkst   
02AE                          ENDIF      
02AE   D1                     POP   DE   
02AF   73                     LD   (HL),E   
02B0   DF           H_DROP:   RST   18h   ; ";" is this one byte
02B1                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
02B1                          IF   CHECKED   
02B1   CD 42 04               CALL   chkst   
02B4                          ENDIF      
02B4   D1                     POP   DE   
02B5   73                     LD   (HL),E   
02B6   23                     INC   HL   
02B7   72                     LD   (HL),D   
02B8   DF                     RST   18h   
02B9                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
02B9                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
02B9   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   HL   
02BA   60                     LD   H,B   
02BB   69                     LD   L,C   
02BC   CD 4B 03               CALL   skipstr   
02BF                          IF   CHECKED   
02BF   B7                     OR   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
02C0   CA B1 04               JP   Z,e_quote   
02C3                          ENDIF      
02C3   F7                     RST   30h   
02C4                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
02C4                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
02C4                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
02C4                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    H_PRINT:   LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   Z,pr9   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,pr1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              AND   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   h_print   
02C4                          ENDIF      
02C4                          IF   CHECKED   
02C4                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
02C4                             ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
02C4                             ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
02C4   E5           H_PRINT:   PUSH   HL   
02C5   CD 82 05               CALL   prstr   
02C8   D1                     POP   DE   
02C9   DF                     RST   18h   
02CA                          ENDIF      
02CA                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                                 ; (With the editor the loop is a routine, prstr, which ^V uses too.)
                    H_PRINT:   CALL   prstr   
                              RST   18h   
02CA                          ENDIF      
02CA   7D           H_EMIT:   LD   A,L   ; "'"
02CB   EF                     RST   28h   
02CC   DF           PR9:      RST   18h   
02CD                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
02CD   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   BC   
02CE   CD 99 03               CALL   psgn   
02D1   C1                     POP   BC   
02D2   DF                     RST   18h   
02D3                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
02D3                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
02D3                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
02D3                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
02D3                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
02D3   CB 7C        H_KEY:    BIT   7,H   
02D5   20 19                  JR   NZ,line   
02D7   1E 28        KT1:      LD   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
02D9   CD F1 03     KT2:      CALL   getk   
02DC   20 0E                  JR   NZ,kt3   
02DE   1D                     DEC   E   
02DF   20 F8                  JR   NZ,kt2   
02E1   7C                     LD   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
02E2   B5                     OR   L   
02E3   28 F2                  JR   Z,kt1   
02E5   2B                     DEC   HL   
02E6   7C                     LD   A,H   
02E7   B5                     OR   L   
02E8   20 ED                  JR   NZ,kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
02EA   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the one byte of ",")
02EB   7E           H_CFETCH:   LD   A,(HL)   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
02EC   6F           KT3:      LD   L,A   
02ED   26 00                  LD   H,0   
02EF   F7                     RST   30h   
02F0                          IF   CPM   
02F0                             ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
02F0                             ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
02F0   11 7F 00     LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
02F3   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
02F4   9F                     SBC   A,A   
02F5   A5                     AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
02F6   EE 7F                  XOR   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
02F8   32 7E 08               LD   (LBHDR),A   
02FB   11 7E 08               LD   DE,LBHDR   
02FE   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
0300   CD 35 04               CALL   bdosx   
0303   21 7F 08               LD   HL,LBHDR+1   
0306   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   ; the count typed (0-127)
0307   2C                     INC   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
0308   85                     ADD   A,L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
0309   6F                     LD   L,A   
030A   36 0D                  LD   (HL),13   
030C                          ENDIF      
030C                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
                                 ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
                                 ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
                                 ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
                                 ; a full line.
                    LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBC   A,A   
                              AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              CPL      
                              LD   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
                                 ;   at most
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   
                    LN2:      CALL   getk   
                              JR   Z,ln2   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,ln5   
                              CP   8   
                              JR   Z,ln4   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,L   
                              CP   D   
                              JR   Z,ln2   ; full
                              LD   (HL),E   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   A,E   
                    LN3:      RST   28h   
                              JR   ln2   
                    LN4:      DEC   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
                              JP   M,ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
                              INC   L   ;   upper half of the page)
                              JR   ln2   
                    LN5:      LD   (HL),A   ; the CR
030C                          ENDIF      
030C   2E 80                  LD   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
030E   F7                     RST   30h   
030F                             ; =============================================================================
030F                             ;  More routines (no handler starts past this point)
030F                             ; =============================================================================
030F                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, DE = remainder.
030F                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. The dividend shifts up through A:C
030F                             ; while the quotient bits arrive at the bottom of C.
030F                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
030F   7B           UDIV:     LD   A,E   
0310   EE 02                  XOR   2   
0312   B2                     OR   D   
0313   20 07                  JR   NZ,udv0   
0315   CB 3C                  SRL   H   
0317   CB 1D                  RR   L   ; the quotient
0319   8F                     ADC   A,A   
031A   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D is 0)
031B   C9                     RET      
031C   7C           UDV0:     LD   A,H   
031D   4D                     LD   C,L   
031E   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
0321   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0323   CB 21        UDV1:     SLA   C   
0325   17                     RLA      
0326   ED 6A                  ADC   HL,HL   
0328   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry is clear here: the remainder
032A   30 02                  JR   NC,udv2   ;   always fits in 16 bits
032C   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; too much: put it back, and cancel the
032D   0D                     DEC   C   ;   INC below
032E   0C           UDV2:     INC   C   ; a quotient bit
032F   10 F2                  DJNZ   udv1   
0331   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = remainder
0332   67                     LD   H,A   
0333   69                     LD   L,C   ; HL = quotient
0334   C9                     RET      
0335                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
0335                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
0335   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LD   HL,0   
0338   0A           RDN1:     LD   A,(BC)   
0339   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
033B   FE 0A                  CP   10   
033D   D0                     RET   NC   
033E   03                     INC   BC   
033F   54                     LD   D,H   
0340   5D                     LD   E,L   
0341   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0342   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0343   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0344   29                     ADD   HL,HL   ; HL * 10
0345   5F                     LD   E,A   
0346   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0348   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0349   18 ED                  JR   rdn1   
034B                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
034B                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
034B                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SS0:      INC   BC   
                    SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
                              INC   BC   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   Z,ss0   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   NZ,skipstr   
                              RET      
034B                          ENDIF      
034B                          IF   CHECKED   
034B                             ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
034B                             ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
034B   0A           SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
034C   B7                     OR   A   
034D   C8                     RET   Z   
034E   03                     INC   BC   
034F   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0351   C8                     RET   Z   
0352   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
0354   20 F5                  JR   NZ,skipstr   
0356   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   ; the escaped character
0357   B7                     OR   A   
0358   C8                     RET   Z   
0359   03                     INC   BC   
035A   18 EF                  JR   skipstr   
035C                          ENDIF      
035C                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
035C                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
035C                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
035C                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
035C                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
035C                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INC that an opener comes back to.
035C                             ; 
035C                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
035C                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
035C                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
035C                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. IX keeps the
035C                             ; place where the skip started, for the report.
035C                SKIP:        
035C                          IF   CHECKED   
035C   C5                     PUSH   BC   
035D   DD E1                  POP   IX   
035F   0B                     DEC   BC   
0360   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0361   03                     INC   BC   
0362   5F                     LD   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
0363                          ENDIF      
0363   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0365   14           SK3:      INC   D   ; an opener: one deeper
0366   0A           SK1:      LD   A,(BC)   
0367                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              INC   BC   
                              OR   A   
                              JP   Z,SKEND   ; (the end of the program)
0367                          ENDIF      
0367                          IF   CHECKED   
0367   B7                     OR   A   
0368   28 22                  JR   Z,sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
036A   03                     INC   BC   
036B                          ENDIF      
036B   FE 22                  CP   22h   
036D   CC 4B 03               CALL   Z,skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
0370   D6 28                  SUB   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
0372   28 F1                  JR   Z,sk3   
0374   3D                     DEC   A   ; ")"
0375   28 08                  JR   Z,sk4   
0377   D6 32                  SUB   "["-")"   
0379   28 EA                  JR   Z,sk3   
037B   FE 02                  CP   "]"-"["   
037D   20 E7                  JR   NZ,sk1   
037F   15           SK4:      DEC   D   
0380                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RET   Z   ; the closer at this level
                              JR   sk1   
0380                          ENDIF      
0380                          IF   CHECKED   
0380   20 E4                  JR   NZ,sk1   
0382   57                     LD   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
0383   AB                     XOR   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
0384   E6 06                  AND   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
0386   FE 02                  CP   2   ;   closer, and only then
0388   7A                     LD   A,D   
0389   C0                     RET   NZ   
038A   18 05                  JR   sk7   
038C   CB 53        SK6:      BIT   2,E   ; the text ran out:
038E   C2 00 00               JP   NZ,SKEND   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
0391   DD E5        SK7:      PUSH   IX   ; N. The place is the opener
0393   C1                     POP   BC   
0394   3E 4E                  LD   A,"N"   
0396   C3 AE 04               JP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
0399                          ENDIF      
0399                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
0399   CB 7C        PSGN:     BIT   7,H   
039B   28 04                  JR   Z,pdec   
039D   3E 2D                  LD   A,"-"   
039F   EF                     RST   28h   
03A0   E7                     RST   20h   
03A1                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
03A1                             ; Uses BC.
03A1   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LD   DE,10   
03A4   CD 0F 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, E = the last digit
03A7   7B                     LD   A,E   
03A8   F5                     PUSH   AF   
03A9   7C                     LD   A,H   
03AA   B5                     OR   L   
03AB   C4 A1 03               CALL   NZ,pdec   
03AE   F1                     POP   AF   
03AF   C6 30                  ADD   A,"0"   
03B1   EF                     RST   28h   
03B2   C9                     RET      
03B3                             ; =============================================================================
03B3                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order
03B3                             ;  (the table itself is the macro PTABLE, defined above the dispatcher).
03B3                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
03B3                             ; =============================================================================
03B3                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
03B3                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
03B3                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
03B3                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
03B3                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
03B3                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
03B3                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
03B3                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
03B3                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
03B3                          IF   1-TABP0   
03B3                PTAB:        
03B3                          ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
03B3   B1                     DB   h_store & 0FFh   
03B4   B9                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   
03B5   CD                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   
03B6   C4                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   
03B7   A9                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
03B8   4C                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   
03B9   CA                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
03BA   28                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   
03BB   30                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   
03BC   6D                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
03BD   43                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   
03BE   EB                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
03BF   3B                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
03C0   AB                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
03C1   81                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   
03C2   A7                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
03C3   B0                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
03C4   54                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
03C5   63                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
03C6   55                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
03C7   D3                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   
03C8   23                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
03C9   FF                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   
03CA   F2                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   
03CB   EE                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
03CC   83                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
03CD   96                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
03CE   D8                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
03CF   2C                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
03D0   8B                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   
03D1   1C                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
03D2   93                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   
03D3                PTABEND:      
03D3                          ENDIF      
03D3                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
03D3                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
03D3                             ; return with the carry clear.
03D3   0A           HEXC:     LD   A,(BC)   
03D4   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
03D6   FE 0A                  CP   10   
03D8   38 09                  JR   C,hc1   
03DA   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   
03DC   D6 11                  SUB   11h   
03DE   FE 06                  CP   6   
03E0   D0                     RET   NC   
03E1   D6 F6                  SUB   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
03E3   03           HC1:      INC   BC   
03E4   C9                     RET      
03E5                             ; =============================================================================
03E5                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
03E5                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
03E5                             ;  (RST 28h) prints A. Both keep BC, DE, HL and HL'. In the generic build
03E5                             ;  they are the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
03E5                             ; 
03E5                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
03E5                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
03E5                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
03E5                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
03E5                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
03E5                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
03E5                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
03E5                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
03E5                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
03E5                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
03E5                             ;  data stack.
03E5                             ; =============================================================================
03E5                          IFN   CPM   
                    RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
03E5                          ENDIF      
03E5                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushn).
03E5   CD 27 04     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
03E8   C8                     RET   Z   ; no key
03E9   32 7A 08               LD   (KEYBUF),A   ; held for the next "?"
03EC   FE 03                  CP   3   
03EE   C0                     RET   NZ   
03EF   18 11                  JR   ctlc   
03F1                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
03F1   E5           GETK:     PUSH   HL   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
03F2   21 7A 08               LD   HL,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
03F5   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
03F6   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
03F8   E1                     POP   HL   
03F9   B7                     OR   A   
03FA   C0                     RET   NZ   
03FB   CD 27 04               CALL   rawk   
03FE   C8                     RET   Z   
03FF   FE 03                  CP   3   
0401   C0                     RET   NZ   
0402                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
0402                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
0402                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
0402                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
0402   3A 7B 08     CTLC:     LD   A,(BRKOFF)   
0405   B7                     OR   A   
0406   CA A6 04               JP   Z,brk   
0409   D5                     PUSH   DE   
040A   11 10 27               LD   DE,250*MSLOOP   
040D   CD 27 04     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
0410   20 05                  JR   NZ,ct2   
0412   1B                     DEC   DE   
0413   7A                     LD   A,D   
0414   B3                     OR   E   
0415   20 F6                  JR   NZ,ct1   
0417   D1           CT2:      POP   DE   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
0418   FE 03                  CP   3   
041A   CA A6 04               JP   Z,brk   
041D   B7                     OR   A   
041E   28 03                  JR   Z,ct3   
0420   32 7A 08               LD   (KEYBUF),A   
0423   3E 03        CT3:      LD   A,3   
0425   B7                     OR   A   
0426   C9                     RET      
0427                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
0427                          ENDIF      ;   (with the editor, both stacks are cleared);
0427                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                    BRK:      EQU   edit0   
0427                          ENDIF      
0427                          IF   CHECKED   
0427                BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
0427                          ENDIF      
0427                          IF   CPM   
0427   3E FF        RAWK:     LD   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
0429                             ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
0429                             ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
0429   D5           PUTC:     PUSH   DE   
042A   E5                     PUSH   HL   
042B   5F                     LD   E,A   
042C   3E 06                  LD   A,6   
042E   CD 35 04               CALL   bdosx   
0431   E1                     POP   HL   
0432   D1                     POP   DE   
0433   B7                     OR   A   ; (for getk)
0434   C9                     RET      
0435                             ; bdosx: call BDOS function A with DE, keeping BC and HL'
0435   C5           BDOSX:    PUSH   BC   
0436   D9                     EXX      
0437   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0438   D9                     EXX      
0439   4F                     LD   C,A   
043A   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
043D   D9                     EXX      
043E   E1                     POP   HL   
043F   D9                     EXX      
0440   C1                     POP   BC   
0441   C9                     RET      
0442                          ENDIF      
0442                             ; =============================================================================
0442                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
0442                             ; =============================================================================
0442                          IF   CHECKED   
0442                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
0442                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
0442                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
0442                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
0442                             ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
0442                             ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
0442                             ; Keeps HL and BC.
0442   23           CHKST:    INC   HL   
0443   7C                     LD   A,H   
0444   2B                     DEC   HL   
0445   FE 08                  CP   LETPAGE   
0447   38 07                  JR   C,chs1   
0449                          ENDIF      
0449                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              RET   C   
0449                          ENDIF      
0449                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0449   5F                     LD   E,A   
044A   3A 07 00               LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
044D   3D                     DEC   A   
044E   BB                     CP   E   
044F   D0                     RET   NC   
0450                          ENDIF      
0450                          IF   CHECKED   
0450   C3 AC 04     CHS1:     JP   e_store   
0453                             ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the old one, the carry is from adding
0453                             ; the count. Stop if the top is not below the limit page, or is below the
0453                             ; program's end.
0453                CHKHP:       
0453                          ENDIF      
0453                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0453                             ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
0453                             ; range, so the add is tested too: growing (A, the count's high
0453                             ; byte, is positive) must not carry, and releasing must.
0453   1F                     RRA      ; the carry comes in above the sign:
0454   C6 40                  ADD   A,40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
0456   87                     ADD   A,A   
0457   38 10                  JR   C,e_heap   
0459   3A 07 00               LD   A,(0007h)   
045C   3D                     DEC   A   
045D   BC                     CP   H   
045E   38 09                  JR   C,e_heap   
0460                          ENDIF      
0460                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                                 ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
                                 ; round always falls outside it.)
                              LD   A,H   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              JR   NC,e_heap   
0460                          ENDIF      
0460                          IF   CHECKED   
0460   D5                     PUSH   DE   
0461   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0462   2A 38 08               LD   HL,(NPEND)   
0465   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; carry: at or above the program's end
0466   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0467   D1                     POP   DE   
0468   D8                     RET   C   
0469   B7           E_HEAP:   OR   A   ; put the count back in TOS for the report
046A   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
046C   C3 A9 04               JP   e_heap1   
046F                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
046F                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
046F                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
046F                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
046F                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
046F                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile. DE is free between characters.
046F   EB           CHKSTK:   EX   DE,HL   
0470   21 05 F8               LD   HL,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
0473   39                     ADD   HL,SP   
0474   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0475   38 1E                  JR   C,e_under   
0477   14                     INC   D   
0478   20 17                  JR   NZ,e_over   
047A   D9                     EXX      ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
047B   7C                     LD   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
047C   FE 06                  CP   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
047E   7D                     LD   A,L   ;   page, in the guard band)
047F   D9                     EXX      
0480   20 0C                  JR   NZ,e_rover   
0482   FE E1                  CP   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
0484   D8                     RET   C   
0485   D9                     EXX      ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
0486   21 E0 06               LD   HL,RSTOP   
0489   D9                     EXX      
048A   3E 72                  LD   A,"r"   
048C   18 20                  JR   errp   
048E   3E 52        E_ROVER:   LD   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
0490   11                     DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides the next entry)
0491   3E 53        E_OVER:   LD   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
0493   18 19                  JR   errp   
0495   31 FC 07     E_UNDER:   LD   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
0498   3E 73                  LD   A,"s"   
049A   18 22                  JR   error   
049C                             ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
049C                             ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a reserved one
049C                             ; in every build (AFh or C3h): if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of
049C                             ; an undefined word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
049C   04           E_HI:     INC   B   
049D   10 17                  DJNZ   e_resv   ; (B is as it was, and is not 0)
049F   CF                     RST   08h   
04A0   42                     LD   B,D   
04A1   4B                     LD   C,E   
04A2   3E 55                  LD   A,"U"   
04A4   18 18                  JR   error   
04A6                             ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
04A6                             ; a 3-byte LD DE,nn (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
04A6   3E 42        E_BREAK:   LD   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
04A8   11                     DB   11h   
04A9   3E 48        E_HEAP1:   LD   A,"H"   ; heap (found inside chkhp)
04AB   11                     DB   11h   
04AC   3E 4F        E_STORE:   LD   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space (chkst)
04AE                             ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
04AE   D1           ERRP:     POP   DE   
04AF   18 0D                  JR   error   
04B1   44           E_QUOTE:   LD   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
04B2   4D                     LD   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
04B3   3E 51                  LD   A,"Q"   
04B5   11                     DB   11h   
04B6   3E 58        E_RESV:   LD   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
04B8   11                     DB   11h   
04B9   3E 5A        E_ZERO:   LD   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
04BB   11                     DB   11h   
04BC   3E 57        E_BRACK:   LD   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
04BE                             ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
04BE                             ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
04BE                             ; 
04BE                             ;   Err X @ line,col
04BE                             ;   up to 16 characters of the text from the place
04BE                             ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
04BE                             ;   Rtn n
04BE   E5           ERROR:    PUSH   HL   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
04BF   5F                     LD   E,A   
04C0   CD 95 05               CALL   pnl   
04C3   45 72 72 20 22         DB   "Err ",22h   
04C8   7B                     LD   A,E   
04C9   EF                     RST   28h   
04CA   CD 9B 05               CALL   pmsg   
04CD   20 40 20 22            DB   " @ ",22h   
04D1   0B                     DEC   BC   ; BC = the place
04D2                             ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
04D2                             ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
04D2                             ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
04D2   21 80 08               LD   HL,LINEBUF   
04D5   11 00 00               LD   DE,0   
04D8   78                     LD   A,B   
04D9   FE 09                  CP   PROG/256   
04DB   38 14                  JR   C,er3   
04DD   24                     INC   H   
04DE   6B                     LD   L,E   ; HL = PROG
04DF   13           ER1:      INC   DE   ; a new line starts at HL
04E0   E5                     PUSH   HL   
04E1   7D           ER2:      LD   A,L   
04E2   91                     SUB   C   
04E3   7C                     LD   A,H   
04E4   98                     SBC   A,B   
04E5   30 09                  JR   NC,er2x   ; reached the place
04E7   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
04E8   23                     INC   HL   
04E9   FE 0A                  CP   10   
04EB   20 F4                  JR   NZ,er2   
04ED   F1                     POP   AF   
04EE   18 EF                  JR   er1   
04F0   E1           ER2X:     POP   HL   
04F1   C5           ER3:      PUSH   BC   
04F2   E5                     PUSH   HL   
04F3   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
04F4   CD A1 03               CALL   pdec   ; the line
04F7   3E 2C                  LD   A,","   
04F9   EF                     RST   28h   
04FA   D1                     POP   DE   
04FB   E1                     POP   HL   
04FC   E5                     PUSH   HL   
04FD   B7                     OR   A   
04FE   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0500   23                     INC   HL   
0501   CD A1 03               CALL   pdec   ; the column
0504   CD 95 05               CALL   pnl   
0507   22                     DB   22h   
0508   E1                     POP   HL   ; the text, as it is: 16 characters, or fewer
0509   06 10                  LD   B,16   ;   if the line or the program ends first
050B   7E           ER4:      LD   A,(HL)   
050C   23                     INC   HL   
050D   B7                     OR   A   
050E   28 0F                  JR   Z,er5   
0510   FE 0D                  CP   13   
0512   28 0B                  JR   Z,er5   
0514   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0516   28 07                  JR   Z,er5   
0518                          ENDIF      
0518                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0518   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   ; (the ^Z that pads a file's last record ends
051A   28 03                  JR   Z,er5   ;   the text too: some terminals clear the
051C                          ENDIF      ;   screen on it)
051C                          IF   CHECKED   
051C   EF                     RST   28h   
051D   10 EC                  DJNZ   er4   
051F                ER5:         ; (without the editor: on into pstk)
051F                          ENDIF      
051F                          IF   CHECKED*EDITOR   
                              CALL   pstk   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              JP   edit0   ; back to the editor, with both stacks cleared
051F                          ENDIF      
051F                             ; =============================================================================
051F                             ;  Routines that the checked build's report and the editor share
051F                             ; =============================================================================
051F                SPADJ:    EQU   2*EDITOR   ; (with the editor pstk is called, not fallen
051F                             ;   into: the stack is one address deeper)
051F                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
051F                             ; pstk: the two stack lines:  Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
051F                             ;                             Rtn n
051F                             ; TOS must be in memory with the rest (pushed). In a build without the
051F                             ; editor this is the end of `error`, which runs on into it.
051F   CD 95 05     PSTK:     CALL   pnl   
0522   53 74 6B 20 22         DB   "Stk ",22h   
0527   21 FA 07               LD   HL,DSTOP-2-SPADJ   ; (the cell at DSTOP-2 was pushed with the
052A   B7                     OR   A   ;   first value and holds nothing)
052B   ED 72                  SBC   HL,SP   
052D   CD 78 05               CALL   phalf   ; the depth
0530   3E 3A                  LD   A,":"   
0532   EF                     RST   28h   
0533   79                     LD   A,C   
0534   FE 09                  CP   9   
0536   38 0A                  JR   C,er6   
0538   CD 9B 05               CALL   pmsg   
053B   20 2E 2E 2E 22         DB   " ...",22h   
0540   0E 08                  LD   C,8   
0542   26 00        ER6:      LD   H,0   ; C = the number of cells to show
0544   69                     LD   L,C   
0545   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0546   39                     ADD   HL,SP   ; HL -> just above the deepest of them
0547                          ENDIF      
0547                          IF   EDITOR   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   HL   
0547                          ENDIF      
0547                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0547   0C                     INC   C   
0548   0D           ER7:      DEC   C   
0549   28 11                  JR   Z,er8   
054B   2B                     DEC   HL   
054C   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
054D   2B                     DEC   HL   
054E   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
054F   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0550   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0551   3E 20                  LD   A," "   
0553   EF                     RST   28h   
0554   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0555   CD 99 03               CALL   psgn   
0558   C1                     POP   BC   
0559   E1                     POP   HL   
055A   18 EC                  JR   er7   
055C   CD 95 05     ER8:      CALL   pnl   
055F   52 74 6E 20 22         DB   "Rtn ",22h   
0564   D9                     EXX      
0565   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0566   D9                     EXX      
0567   D1                     POP   DE   
0568   21 E0 06               LD   HL,RSTOP   
056B   B7                     OR   A   
056C   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
056E                          ENDIF      
056E                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
056E   CD 78 05               CALL   phalf   
0571   CD 95 05               CALL   pnl   
0574   22                     DB   22h   
0575   C3 15 01               JP   endprog   
0578                          ENDIF      
0578                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0578                             ; phalf: print half of HL, and leave it in C. (With the editor, pstk ends by
0578                             ; running on into this.)
0578   CB 3C        PHALF:    SRL   H   
057A   CB 1D                  RR   L   
057C   E5                     PUSH   HL   
057D   CD A1 03               CALL   pdec   
0580   C1                     POP   BC   
0581   C9                     RET      
0582                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
0582                             ; "$", and the texts of the report and the editor). In the checked build a
0582                             ; NUL first is an error: Q.
0582   7E           PRSTR:    LD   A,(HL)   
0583   23                     INC   HL   
0584   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0586   C8                     RET   Z   
0587                          ENDIF      
0587                          IF   CHECKED   
0587   B7                     OR   A   
0588   28 17                  JR   Z,e_dollar   
058A                          ENDIF      
058A                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
058A   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
058C   20 04                  JR   NZ,prs1   
058E   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
058F   23                     INC   HL   
0590   E6 BF                  AND   0BFh   
0592   EF           PRS1:     RST   28h   
0593   18 ED                  JR   prstr   
0595                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
0595                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
0595   3E 0D        PNL:      LD   A,13   
0597   EF                     RST   28h   
0598   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
059A   EF                     RST   28h   
059B   E3           PMSG:     EX   (SP),HL   
059C   CD 82 05               CALL   prstr   
059F   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   
05A0   C9                     RET      
05A1                          ENDIF      
05A1                          IF   CHECKED   
05A1   D1           E_DOLLAR:   POP   DE   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop the return address,
05A2   E1                     POP   HL   ;   and put the string's address back in TOS
05A3   3E 51                  LD   A,"Q"   
05A5   C3 BE 04               JP   error   
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                             ; =============================================================================
05A8                             ;  The line editor (EDITOR = 1)
05A8                             ; 
05A8                             ;  The interpreter starts here, and a program that ends comes back here.
05A8                             ;  There is no prompt. It follows the spec's suggested standard for a line
05A8                             ;  editor (docs/b8script.md, Environments). Type a line and press Return:
05A8                             ; 
05A8                             ;    n text    put the text in as line n; the lines from n on move down. A
05A8                             ;              number past the end (or 0) adds the line at the end.
05A8                             ;    n         take line n out
05A8                             ;    anything else is run at once, as B8Script. (Start such a line with a
05A8                             ;    space if it would begin with a digit.)
05A8                             ; 
05A8                             ;  A command key ends the line too, and takes what was typed as its argument:
05A8                             ; 
05A8                             ;    ^G        run the program
05A8                             ;    n ^L      list from line n (no number: all of it). Any key holds the
05A8                             ;              list until another key is pressed; Ctrl-C ends it.
05A8                             ;    n ^E      put line n in the input line; Return puts it back, changed
05A8                             ;    name ^R   read. CP/M: the file of that name (no name: the same file as
05A8                             ;              last time). Generic: what is typed, or pasted, from now until
05A8                             ;              ^Z replaces the program; it is not echoed.
05A8                             ;    name ^W   write. CP/M: to that file (no name: the same file as last
05A8                             ;              time). Generic: the text is printed, as it is.
05A8                             ;    ^N ^N     new: no program (the key twice in a row)
05A8                             ;    ^V        view: the build, both stacks, and the program's size, lines
05A8                             ;              and free memory
05A8                             ;    ^X        leave (to LEAVE)
05A8                             ; 
05A8                             ;  In the line: ^B and ^F, or the left and right arrow keys, move the cursor;
05A8                             ;  a character goes in at the cursor; Backspace and DEL take out the one
05A8                             ;  before it; Esc drops the line. Only CR, LF, BS and printing characters are
05A8                             ;  sent to the terminal, so any terminal will do.
05A8                             ; 
05A8                             ;  Lines are counted, not numbered: the text holds no line numbers, and the
05A8                             ;  list shows each line's place. There can be 65535 lines. A typed line holds
05A8                             ;  125 characters; the one character after a line number separates it from
05A8                             ;  the text and is not stored. The text is kept as it is typed, each line
05A8                             ;  ending in CR LF, at PROG.
05A8                             ; 
05A8                             ;  What lasts from one line to the next: the program, the words, the
05A8                             ;  variables and the data stack. An error or a break clears both stacks. The
05A8                             ;  return stack starts empty for every line.
05A8                             ; 
05A8                             ;  Things to know:
05A8                             ;    - Reset empties the program (generic builds).
05A8                             ;    - A word's address points into the program, so run the program again
05A8                             ;      after editing it.
05A8                             ;    - Nothing is printed between a program's output and what is typed next.
05A8                             ;    - A line run at once sits in the line buffer, which -n? also reads into:
05A8                             ;      a line that calls -n? and carries on afterwards runs what was typed.
05A8                             ;      (The stored program never comes back to the line, so it may.)
05A8                             ;    - The editor"s own keys are not the program"s: -n? is the plain line
05A8                             ;      read of the other builds (BDOS 10 under CP/M).
05A8                             ; 
05A8                             ;  The data stack is the CPU's stack, so the editor works on top of whatever
05A8                             ;  the last line left there, with TOS pushed like the rest.
05A8                             ; =============================================================================
05A8                          IF   EDGEN   
                    INIT:        ; reset (A = 0)
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDGEN*CHECKED   
                                 ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at 0, and
                                 ; every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is caught at
                                 ; (see e_hi).
                              LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDGEN   
                              JR   edit0   
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDITOR   
                                 ; ^B, left arrow: the cursor goes one to the left
                    LEFT:     LD   A,L   
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; (L = 80h: at the start)
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   A,8   
                    LF1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; ^F, right arrow: one to the right, by printing the character there
                    RIGHT:    LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; at the end
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   lf1   
                                 ; Esc: alone it drops the line. An arrow key sends Esc [ and a letter, so
                                 ; wait about 5 ms for a second key: after a "[" read on to the letter that
                                 ; ends the sequence, and act on C (right) and D (left).
                    ESC:      LD   BC,5*MSLOOP   
                    ES1:      CALL   rawk   
                              JR   NZ,es2   
                              DEC   BC   
                              LD   A,B   
                              OR   C   
                              JR   NZ,es1   
                              CALL   fin   ; no second key: the line is dropped
                              JR   edit   
                    ES2:      CP   "["   
                              JR   NZ,ed1   ; not a sequence known here
                    ES3:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   40h   
                              JR   C,es3   ; (its parameters)
                              CP   "C"   
                              JR   Z,right   
                              CP   "D"   
                              JR   Z,left   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; edit0: reset, an error or a break: both stacks are cleared.
                                 ; skend: a program that ended inside skip: its return address goes.
                                 ; edend: a program that ended: TOS joins the rest of the data stack.
                    EDIT0:    LD   SP,DSTOP-2   ; empty (the cell that stands for TOS is pushed)
                              DB   21h   ; (LD HL,nn: steps over the next two bytes)
                    SKEND:    POP   DE   
                    EDEND:    PUSH   HL   
                                 ; edit: start a new input line.
                    EDIT:     EXX      
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
                              EXX      
                              LD   HL,0   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
                              LD   (EDLN),HL   ; no line is being edited
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; HL = the cursor,
                              LD   E,L   ;   E = the end of the line (its low byte)
                    ED1:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   7Fh   
                              JR   Z,bsp   ; DEL
                              CP   " "   
                              JR   NC,insc   
                              CP   9   
                              JR   Z,insc   ; Tab is text
                              CP   8   
                              JR   Z,bsp   
                              CP   2   
                              JR   Z,left   ; ^B
                              CP   6   
                              JR   Z,right   ; ^F
                              CP   1Bh   
                              JR   Z,esc   
                              PUSH   HL   ; a command key? Look it up
                              LD   HL,cmds   
                              LD   B,NCMD   
                    ED2:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   Z,ed3   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   ed2   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   ed1   ; no: the key is ignored
                    ED3:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   H,(HL)   
                              LD   L,A   
                              EX   (SP),HL   ; the command's address: fin returns to it
                                 ; fin: end the input line: CR LF and a NUL after it, and a new line on the
                                 ; terminal. Leaves BC -> the line and HL -> the NUL.
                    FIN:      LD   H,LETPAGE   
                              LD   L,E   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              DEC   L   
                              CALL   prl   ; (prints the CR LF)
                              LD   (HL),0   
                              LD   BC,LINEBUF   
                              RET      
                                 ; Backspace, DEL: the character before the cursor goes. The cursor moves
                                 ; left, the rest of the line moves down over it, and the last place (now a
                                 ; space) is printed over along with the rest.
                    BSP:      LD   A,L   
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; at the start
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   A,8   
                              RST   28h   
                              PUSH   HL   
                    BS1:      INC   L   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   NZ,bs1   
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   (HL)," "   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   D,E   
                              DEC   E   
                              JR   ic2   
                                 ; A character goes in at the cursor: it ripples up through the rest of the
                                 ; line, the cursor moves on, and the rest is printed again.
                    INSC:     LD   B,A   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   0FDh   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; the line is full: 125 characters
                              LD   A,B   
                              RST   28h   
                              PUSH   HL   
                    IC1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              LD   (HL),B   
                              LD   B,A   
                              LD   A,L   
                              INC   L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   NZ,ic1   
                              POP   HL   
                              INC   L   
                              INC   E   
                              LD   D,E   
                    IC2:      CALL   tail   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; tail: print the line from the cursor to D (a low byte), and bring the
                                 ; cursor back with backspaces. Nothing at all if the cursor is at D.
                    TAIL:     LD   C,L   
                    TA1:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   D   
                              JR   Z,ta2   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   ta1   
                    TA2:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   C   
                              RET   Z   
                              LD   A,8   
                              RST   28h   
                              DEC   L   
                              JR   ta2   
                                 ; ekey: wait for a key
                    EKEY:     CALL   rawk   
                              JR   Z,ekey   
                              RET      
                                 ; The command keys, and where each goes (after fin).
                    CMDS:     DB   13   
                              DW   cret   
                              DB   7   ; ^G
                              DW   crun   
                              DB   12   ; ^L
                              DW   clist   
                              DB   5   ; ^E
                              DW   cedln   
                              DB   18   ; ^R
                              DW   cread   
                              DB   23   ; ^W
                              DW   cwrite   
                              DB   14   ; ^N
                              DW   cnew   
                              DB   22   ; ^V
                              DW   cview   
                              DB   24   ; ^X
                              DW   LEAVE   
                    NCMD:     EQU   9   
                                 ; ^N ^N: no program, if the next key is ^N too
                    CNEW:     CALL   ekey   
                              CP   14   
                              JR   NZ,ged0   
                              XOR   A   
                              LD   (PROG),A   
                    GED0:     JP   edit   
                                 ; ^E: line n goes into the input line, to be changed. EDLN remembers which
                                 ; line it was: Return puts the text back in its place.
                    CEDLN:    CALL   rdnum   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   find   ; HL -> the line, or the NUL if there is none
                              POP   DE   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ged0   
                              LD   (EDLN),DE   
                              LD   DE,LINEBUF   
                    CE1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,ce2   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,ce2   
                              LD   (DE),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   E   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   0FDh   ; (a longer line is cut at 125 characters)
                              JR   NZ,ce1   
                    CE2:      LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; show it; the cursor ends up at its end
                    CE3:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JP   Z,ed1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   ce3   
                                 ; Return. If ^E put a line here, the text goes back in its place. If not:
                                 ; a number and text is a line to put in, a number alone a line to take out,
                                 ; and anything else is run where it is.
                    CRET:     PUSH   HL   ; the end of what was typed
                              LD   HL,(EDLN)   
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JR   Z,cr1   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   delln   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   ins   
                    CR1:      CALL   rdnum   ; HL = the number it starts with, BC -> after
                              LD   A,C   ; C is still 80h if there was no number:
                              ADD   A,A   ;   only then is twice it 0
                              JR   Z,st0p   ; no number: run the line
                              LD   A,(BC)   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   NZ,cr2   
                              POP   DE   ; the number alone: take that line out
                              CALL   delln   
                              JR   gedit   
                    CR2:      INC   BC   ; step over the one character after the number
                                 ; Put the text at BC in as line n (in HL): open a gap of its length there,
                                 ; CR and LF included, and copy it in.
                    INS:      CALL   find   ; HL -> where it goes
                              POP   DE   ; the end of what was typed
                              LD   A,E   
                              SUB   C   ; A = the length of the text, with its CR LF
                              PUSH   BC   ; the text
                              LD   C,A   
                              LD   B,0   
                              PUSH   BC   ; its length
                              LD   D,H   
                              LD   E,L   ; DE = where it goes
                              XOR   A   
                              LD   C,A   ; BC = 0: CPIR looks as far as it needs to
                              CPIR      ; HL -> one past the program's NUL
                              SBC   HL,DE   ; the number of bytes to move up, NUL included
                              LD   B,H   
                              LD   C,L   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              EX   (SP),HL   ; HL = the length; where it goes is kept
                              PUSH   HL   
                              ADD   HL,DE   ; the NUL's new place
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              LDDR      ; move the rest of the program up
                              POP   BC   ; the length
                              POP   DE   ; where it goes
                              POP   HL   ; the text
                              LDIR      
                    GEDIT:    JP   edit   
                                 ; ^G: run the program. st0p: run the typed line (BC -> it).
                    CRUN:     LD   BC,PROG   
                              DB   3Eh   ; (LD A,n: steps over the POP)
                    ST0P:     POP   HL   ; (the end of what was typed)
                                 ; st0: start running at BC. The heap starts after the stored program's NUL.
                    ST0:      LD   HL,PROG   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
                              LD   (HEAP),HL   
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDITOR*CHECKED   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDITOR   
                              POP   HL   ; TOS: the data stack is as the last line left it
                              RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
                                 ; ^L: list from line n. DE = the number of the line at HL.
                    CLIST:    CALL   rdnum   ; HL = n, or 0 if there was none:
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JR   NZ,li0   
                              INC   L   ;   then from line 1
                    LI0:      PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   find   
                              POP   DE   
                    LI1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,gedit   ; the end of the text
                              CALL   rawk   
                              JR   Z,li3   ; no key: carry on
                              CP   3   
                              JR   Z,gedit   ; Ctrl-C
                              CALL   ekey   ; any other key: wait for one more
                              CP   3   
                              JR   Z,gedit   
                    LI3:      PUSH   HL   
                              PUSH   DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the line's number,
                              LD   A," "   
                              RST   28h   ;   a space,
                              POP   DE   
                              POP   HL   
                              INC   DE   
                              CALL   prl   ;   and the line
                              JR   li1   
                                 ; ^V: view.
                    CVIEW:    CALL   pmsg   
                              DB   "B8SZ80E"   
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDITOR*CHECKED   
                              DB   "C"   
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDITOR   
                              DB   " 2026-11-21",22h   
                              CALL   pstk   ; both stacks
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                              LD   DE,0   
                    CV1:      LD   A,(HL)   ; count the lines, and find the end
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,cv2   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,cv1   
                              INC   DE   
                              JR   cv1   
                    CV2:      PUSH   HL   ; the NUL
                              PUSH   DE   ; the lines
                              LD   DE,(0-PROG)&0FFFFh   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Prog ",22h   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the program's size
                              POP   HL   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Lines ",22h   
                              CALL   pdec   
                              POP   DE   
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDGEN   
                              LD   HL,HEAPLIM*256-1   
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the limit
                              LD   H,A   
                              LD   L,0   
                              DEC   HL   
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDITOR   
                              OR   A   
                              SBC   HL,DE   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Free ",22h   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the room left for text and heap
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                    GED1:     JP   edit   
                                 ; delln: take line n (in HL) out: copy everything after it down over it.
                    DELLN:    CALL   find   
                              LD   D,H   
                              LD   E,L   
                              CALL   nxl   ; HL -> the next line
                    DE1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              LD   (DE),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   DE   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   NZ,de1   
                              RET      
                                 ; find: HL = a line number. Returns HL -> that line, or -> the NUL at the end
                                 ; of the text if there are fewer lines (or the number is 0). Keeps BC.
                    FIND:     EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                    FI1:      DEC   DE   
                              LD   A,D   
                              OR   E   
                              RET   Z   
                              CALL   nxl   
                              JR   NZ,fi1   
                              RET      
                                 ; nxl: step HL over one line, to just past its LF (and return not-zero), or
                                 ; stop at the NUL that ends the text (and return zero).
                    NXL:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,nxl   
                              OR   A   
                              RET      
                                 ; prl: print the line at HL, to its LF; HL -> just past it.
                    PRL:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,prl   
                              RET      
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDGEN   
                                 ; ^R, generic: what comes in from now until ^Z is the program. A CR is
                                 ; stored as CR LF; a LF right after a line end is dropped (it is the CR's
                                 ; own, or an empty line's), and a LF anywhere else ends a line too. A last
                                 ; line with no end is given one. Nothing is echoed, and there is no check
                                 ; for running out of memory.
                    CREAD:    LD   HL,PROG-1   
                              LD   A,10   
                              DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the LD A,13)
                    RD1:      LD   A,13   ; a LF alone ends a line
                    RD2:      LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   13   
                              LD   A,10   
                              JR   Z,rd2   ; after a CR goes a LF
                    RD3:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   Z,rd4   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,rd2   
                              DEC   HL   
                              CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   Z,rd3   ; (the LF is dropped)
                              JR   rd1   
                    RD4:      DEC   HL   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,rd5   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              INC   HL   
                    RD5:      LD   (HL),0   
                              JR   ged1   
                                 ; ^W, generic: the text is printed as it is, for the terminal to capture.
                    CWRITE:   LD   HL,PROG   
                    CW1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ged1   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   cw1   
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    CFCB:     EQU   005Ch   ; the file's name is kept here, where the CCP
                                 ;   put the one from the command line
                                 ; ^R, CP/M: read the file. A name typed before the key is the file's name
                                 ; from now on.
                    CREAD:    CALL   setname   
                              CALL   load   
                              JP   edit   
                                 ; ^W, CP/M: write the file: delete the old one, make it anew, write the
                                 ; text in records of 128 bytes, and close it. The text's NUL and the 127
                                 ; bytes after it are set to ^Z meanwhile, which pads the last record.
                    CWRITE:   CALL   setname   
                              CALL   fcbclr   
                              LD   C,19   ; delete
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              LD   C,22   ; make
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              INC   A   
                              JP   Z,edit   ; no room in the directory
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                              XOR   A   
                    CW1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,cw1   
                              DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   B,128   
                    CW2:      LD   (HL),1Ah   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   cw2   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   DE,PROG   
                    CW3:      LD   A,E   ; a record that starts before the end is written
                              SUB   L   
                              LD   A,D   
                              SBC   A,H   
                              JR   NC,cw4   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              PUSH   DE   
                              LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address: the record is written
                              CALL   BDOS   ;   from where it lies
                              LD   C,21   ; write
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   DE,128   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   cw3   
                    CW4:      LD   (HL),0   ; the NUL again
                              LD   C,16   ; close
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              JP   edit   
                                 ; setname: if a name was typed (the line does not start with its CR), put it
                                 ; in the CFCB: up to 8 characters, a dot, up to 3 more, in capitals. The drive
                                 ; is the current one.
                    SETNAME:   LD   DE,LINEBUF   
                              LD   A,(DE)   
                              CP   13   
                              RET   Z   
                              LD   HL,CFCB   
                              LD   (HL),0   ; the current drive
                              LD   B,11   
                    SN1:      INC   L   
                              LD   (HL)," "   
                              DJNZ   sn1   
                              LD   L,CFCB+1   
                    SN2:      LD   A,(DE)   
                              INC   DE   
                              CP   13   
                              RET   Z   
                              CP   "."   
                              JR   NZ,sn3   
                              LD   L,CFCB+9   ; the type
                              JR   sn2   
                    SN3:      CP   "a"   
                              JR   C,sn4   
                              AND   5Fh   ; a capital
                    SN4:      LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   sn2   
                                 ; fcbclr: clear the CFCB after its name, as it must be before a file is opened
                    FCBCLR:   LD   HL,CFCB+12   
                              LD   B,24   
                    FC1:      LD   (HL),0   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   fc1   
                              RET      
                                 ; fbdos: BDOS function C on the file
                    FBDOS:    LD   DE,CFCB   
                              JP   BDOS   
                                 ; load: read the file into PROG. No such file: no program. The text ends at
                                 ; the file"s first ^Z (1Ah), which pads a text file"s last record; one more
                                 ; goes after the last record, so the search always stops. And every line
                                 ; must end in LF: a last line without one is given a CR LF.
                    LOAD:     CALL   fcbclr   
                              LD   C,15   ; open (no such file: the first read fails
                              CALL   fbdos   ;   too)
                              LD   DE,PROG   
                    LD1:      PUSH   DE   
                              LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              LD   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              POP   HL   ; HL = the address this record went to
                              OR   A   
                              JR   NZ,ld2   
                              LD   DE,128   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              JR   ld1   
                    LD2:      LD   (HL),1Ah   
                              LD   HL,PROG-1   
                              LD   A,10   ; (a file with no text needs nothing added)
                    TR1:      INC   HL   
                              LD   E,A   ; E = the character before this one
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,tr1   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,tr2   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              INC   HL   
                    TR2:      LD   (HL),0   
                              RET      
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                             ; =============================================================================
05A8                             ;  CP/M startup (the generic build starts at address 0: see st0)
05A8                             ; =============================================================================
05A8                          IF   CPM   
05A8                             ; The RAM pages follow the image; the heap may grow to the BDOS.
05A8                START:       
05A8                          ENDIF      
05A8                          IF   CPM*CHECKED   
05A8                             ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at
05A8                             ; 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is
05A8                             ; caught at (see e_hi: the byte there is CP/M's JP, C3h), and no key
05A8                             ; is held back.
05A8   21 00 08               LD   HL,LET   
05AB   AF                     XOR   A   
05AC   77           INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
05AD   2C                     INC   L   
05AE   F2 AC 05               JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
05B1                          ENDIF      
05B1                          IF   CPM   
05B1   21 08 01               LD   HL,vecs   ; the RST routines go down into page zero
05B4   11 08 00               LD   DE,0008h   
05B7   01 2C 00               LD   BC,vecend-vecs   
05BA   ED B0                  LDIR      
05BC                          ENDIF      
05BC                          IF   CPM*EDITOR   
                              CALL   load   ; the file named on the command line
                              JP   edit0   
05BC                          ENDIF      
05BC                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
05BC   11 5C 00               LD   DE,005Ch   ; open the file named on the command line
05BF   0E 0F                  LD   C,15   ; (no such file: the first read fails too,
05C1   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   ;   and the program is empty)
05C4   11 00 09               LD   DE,PROG   
05C7   D5           LD1:      PUSH   DE   
05C8   0E 1A                  LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address
05CA   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
05CD   11 5C 00               LD   DE,005Ch   
05D0   0E 14                  LD   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
05D2   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
05D5   E1                     POP   HL   ; HL = the address this record went to
05D6   B7                     OR   A   
05D7   20 07                  JR   NZ,ld2   
05D9   11 80 00               LD   DE,128   
05DC   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
05DD   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
05DE   18 E7                  JR   ld1   
05E0   36 00        LD2:      LD   (HL),0   ; the end of the file counts as NUL
05E2   23                     INC   HL   ; the heap starts after it
05E3   01 00 09               LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
05E6   C3 76 01               JP   st2   
05E9                          ENDIF      
05E9                          IF   CPM   
05E9                             ; RAM pages, after the image
05E9                RSPAGE:   EQU   (imgend + 255) / 256   
05E9                DSPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 1   
05E9                LETPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 2   
05E9                PROG:     EQU   LETPAGE*256 + 256   
05E9                          ENDIF      
05E9                IMGEND:      


